footer  (carry, after the build, the finish's sentence standing) [green] Built 2 parts, RangeBox_r2_Layout, RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier and RangeBox_r2.SLDASM, reusing the 4 parts already built; no interference between the gears in any mode, where they stand. Its turning gears are mated to turn in each of its 3 modes, one configuration each (H, N and L), and SolidWorks reports no mate in error in any of them: it opens in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. RangeSlv slides along Output, to its place in each mode. The 3 copies of Planet turn on Carrier, and RangeBox_r2_Carrier_Carrier holds Carrier's axes and planes only: a plate and pins are yours to add. Ring stays fixed where it is placed: its shaft does not turn. A turn you give the gears in one mode can show in other modes, so a dog can stand across its sleeve in another; to put the gears back there, press Update SolidWorks with that mode showing. 1 thing to do by hand: Assign a material to each of the 2 parts; the build leaves it unset. Carried into RangeBox_r2, unsaved: your Sprocket-1 (was Sprocket-2), Sprocket-2 (was Sprocket-1), Sprocket-3 (was Sprocket-9) and 14 other components, each where it stood, and 25 of your 31 mates, each on in the modes it was on in. UserAsm6 is on a plane of RangeBox.SLDASM itself, which Gear Generator did not read while SprocketLight-1 was lightweight in it, so it is not made again. UserAxis9 is on Sprocket-9, which is suppressed in H, the mode RangeBox.SLDASM showed, so it could not be read and is not made again. UserSunFace was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. UserGearFillet was on a face of Sun, and Sun's part is new because its Flank changed, so it is not made again. UserAxisLight is on SprocketLight-1, which was lightweight in RangeBox.SLDASM, so what it joins could not be read, and it is not made again. Your User Keyway Sketch and User Keyway stay in Gear_m1.25_N29, which Sun's new part replaces because its Flank changed (RangeBox.SLDASM and that file keep them). Housing-1 and Sprocket-9 (was Sprocket-8) are fixed where they stood in RangeBox_r2: with your UserLock8a made again SolidWorks reads Sun unable to turn, so it was not kept; UserAngle8b beside it was. Your components were placed where they stood in H, the mode RangeBox.SLDASM showed; one no mate holds stands there in every mode. Assembly features, display states and appearances stay behind; pattern instances come over as components of their own. If a part of yours was made in context of RangeBox.SLDASM, it still refers to that assembly's parts. SprocketLight-1 was lightweight in RangeBox.SLDASM and is resolved there now: SolidWorks loaded its part to carry it. Save RangeBox_r2 in SolidWorks to keep what was carried.
        button 'Build again…' on; Update SolidWorks shown on primary
footer  (carry, after the build, the finish's sentence gone) [green] SolidWorks already matches the workbook on record; Update SolidWorks checks it live and puts right anything changed there; gears turned in SolidWorks stay where they are unless something must move. It was built with a configuration per mode (H, N and L), each named as its mode, and saved in H; to switch mode, double-click another mode's configuration in SolidWorks' ConfigurationManager. Drag Sun in SolidWorks and the rest of its train follow. Carrier (the carrier) is axes and planes only, so it has nothing to drag. As read at 07:10, Update SolidWorks leaves your Sprocket-1, Sprocket-2, Sprocket-3, 14 other components and 25 mates as they are. RangeBox_r2 holds what Build again… carried of yours, not saved: save it in SolidWorks to keep it.
